title: The WTB Debate
subtitle: Wladimir Woytinsky and the ADGB have presented a proposal.
view-if: black_thursday_seen and wtb_support > 3
tags: event
new-page: true
on-arrival:{! crisis_urgency += 1; wtb_proposed = 1
Q.wtb_score = 0;
Q.centrist_score = 0;
Q.leftist_score = 0;

if (Q.spd_in_goverment == 0) {
    leftist_score += 2;
}
leftist_score += 1 if spd_relation < 50
leftist_score += 2 if spd_relation < 25

if (Q.in_grand_coalition) {
centrist_score += 4;
wtb_score -= 1;
leftist_score -= 2;
}

if (Q.unemployed > 15) {
    leftist_score += 1;
    wtb_score += 1;
}

if (Q.z_ideology == "Left") {
    wtb_score += 2;
    centrist_score -= 1;
}

if (Q.z_leader == "Kaiser") {
    wtb_score += 3;
    leftist_score += 1;
}

if (Q.budget < 0) {
    centrist_score += 2;
}

if (Q.in_weimar_coalition) {
    wtb_score += 2;
}

if (Q.kpd_leader == "Conciliators") {
    leftist_score += 2;
    centrist_score -= 1;
}

if (Q.in_popular_front) {
    leftist_score += 3;
    wtb_score += 1;
    centrist_score -= 3;
}
if (Q.in_left_front) {
    leftist_score += 20;
    centrist_score -= 50;
}
if (Q.neorevisionism_spd == 1) {
    wtb_score += 1;
    centrist_score -= 1;

wtb_plan_yay = 1 if wtb_score > centrist_score and wtb_score > leftist_score;
wtp_plan_nay = 1 if centrist_score > wtb_score and centrist_score > leftist_score;
leftis_plan_woo = 1 if leftist_score > wtb_score and leftist_score > centrist_score;
wtb_plan nay = 1 if (centrist score = wtb_score = leftist_score);
}
on-display: {!  
    var cardEl = document.createElement('div');  
    cardEl.className = "face-figure2";  

    var image = new Image();  
    image.className = "face-img";  
    image.src = "img/wtb_gang.jpg";  

    cardEl.appendChild(image);  
    var contentDiv = document.querySelector("#page #mid_panel #content");
    contentDiv.appendChild(cardEl);
!}

= The WTB Plan

Following Woytinsky's announcement of intentions to draft a national action plan to stimulate the economy through extensive public works, he, Tarnow, and Baade have presented the WTB Plan, named after them, to the ADGB and <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD**</span> leadership. While the ADGB has shown enthusiasm and formally adopted the plan, the <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD**</span>'s economic expert, Rudolf Hilferding, along with Rudolf Breitscheid and party leader Otto Wels, are much more resistant, showing significant skepticism.

The fear of inflation caused by funding the plan through public works, especially with hyperinflation still fresh in memory, and the unwillingness to "play doctor at the bedside of capitalism," are the main reasons for the Centrists' reluctance. Maybe they can be convinced?

- @wtb_vote: The party votes...

@wtb_vote

- @center_plan
- @leftist_plan
- @wtb_plan

@center_plan
title: The WTB-Plan is rejected!
subtitle: Nothing ever happens.
choose-if: wtb_plan_nay == 1
unavailable-subtitle: [? if z_ideology == "Left": Our cooperative leadership has given them confidence in the possibility of the Plan's enaction. ?] the WTB-Plan's supoort is overwhelming among the base and ADGB.

the Center wing, primarily led by Orthodox Marxist economist Rudolf Hilferding, has come out victorious in rejecting the WTB-Plan. They argue that [? if z_ideology != Left: the plan will never make it through the Reichstag due to the hostility of the bourgeois parties, ?] the Plan is a band-aid to capitalism and that the inflation caused by the plan will cause greater suffering among the people. The <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD**</span>'s current position of waiting for capitalism to collapse if maintained.

@wtb_plan
title: The <span style="color: #000000;">W</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">T</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">B</span>-Plan is adopted!
choose-if: wtb_plan_yay == 1
unavailable-subtitle: [? if z_ideology != "Left": The plan's enaction seems hopeless, looking at the <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD**</span>'s current coalition partners.?] The Center faction is able to convince the rest of the party against the Plan.
on-arrival: wtb_adopted = 1; workers_spd += 5; unemployed_spd += 6; new_middle_spd += 3

the ADGB, and the masterminds behind the WTB-Plan, Woytinsky, Tarnow and Baade are able to convince the party into adopting the WTB-Plan! The base is glad to see that the <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD**</span> is taking action against the Crisis, reinvogarating support.

@leftist_plan
title: the... Left Plan is adopted?
choose-if: leftist_plan_woo == 1
unavailable-subtitle: The Left faction is not strong enough. The <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD**</span> is too commited to reform. The <span style="color: #000000;">W</span><span style="color: #DD0000;">T</span><span style="color: #FFCC00;">B</span>-Plan has taken the spotlight.
subtitle: Huh?
on-arrival: workers_spd += 8; unemployed_spd += 8; new_middle_spd -= 5; old_middle_spd -= 5; spd_relation -= 10 if z_leader != "Kaiser"

Suprisingly, the division between the Center and Labor, combined with [? if in_popular_front or in_left_front: the <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD**</span>'s cooperation with the <span style="color: #700000;">**KPD**</span> in national goverment,?][? if spd_in_government == 0; The <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD**</span>'s exclusion from goverment,?] The radicalization caused by the Crisis and the rise of the <span style="color: #700000;">**KPD**</span> in the polls has led to the Left Plan, advocating for agressive nationalizations and class war, being adopted as the <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD**</span>'s economic plan. This has led to increased support from the proletariat and backlas from the middle classes. [? if z_leader != Kaiser: Our relations are strained with the <span style="color: #c00000;">**SPD**</span>, as their rhetoric increasingly targets us as one of the "bourgeois" parties and enemy of the working class. ?]
